      },
      "isNameUserDefined": true,
      "description": "Galatea is a small, rocky world orbiting extremely close to Phanes. Due to its proximity, it is slightly egg-shaped. It has a dark coloration, and Drilling Missions indicate that it is made of Basalt, formed when lava cools extremely fast. It's likely that, in Galatea's past, a giant resurfacing event occurred when a large asteroid collided with the small moon, liquefying its surface. This event likely happened during the moon's formation, as hundreds of craters are present on its surface. Galatea also has a minor effect on Phane's rings. causing wave patterns in its wake."
    },
