      },
      "isNameUserDefined": true,
      "description": "Hestia is the 2nd moon of Phanes and the 4th largest; its surface is extremely similar to Io's, with hundreds of active volcanoes dotting the small moon. This volcanic activity is fueled by the immense gravity of its parent planet, which tugs on the moon. Its nearby sibling moons also tug on Hestia; this heats the interior to immense levels, creating a giant molten subsurface ocean of magma. This magma wells up and creates, you guessed it! Volcanos. Hestia is one of the most volcanically active bodies in the Alpha Centauri system.",
      "description_playerhidden": false
    },
