      },
      "isNameUserDefined": true,
      "description": "The Farthest moon of Phanes, Ptolemy, is a bit smaller than its twin, Pandora; however, they are very different. Ptolemy's only inhabitants on land are primitive plants. Ptolemy obviously hasn't had life for as long as Pandora has, even with the plants on land; oxygen levels are still low but have been increasing over time. However, the oceans are full of life, with multiple habitats, from the sun-soaked bays and reefs closer to land to the abyssal plains where little light reaches; a nice place to refuel before venturing off into the depths of space."
