      "image": {
        "url": "/images/planet_types/web20habitable20planet.jpg"
      },
      "description": " Bathed in the warm light of its star, Persephone is an Earth-like planet smaller than Earth, hosting a Primitive ecosystem. There is no life on land, the air is unbreathable due to excess carbon dioxide, and the only visible organisms in the water are vast mats of cyanobacteria covering coastal rocks. And it'll likely stay like that for the next 400 million years without human intervention. However, with a mask, you may last long enough on land to see its two moons in the sky, Panoptes and Melinoe. However, Persephone may be on the verge of entering an oxygenation event due to the abundance of cyanobacteria, which would turn its oceans blood red as the iron dissolved in them would be oxidized. thus, paving the way for complex life on Persephone."
    },
